{"id": "v19-err-flow-capability-refusal",
 "asserts": "From rung 3 on, what an older Rust recording is missing when it is asked about `Err` flow is a RECORD, not a rule -- so `exceptions` refuses it through the capability, with the standard `caps.require` sentence and exit 3, and the reader's next move is to record again under a runtime that produces err-flow records. The gate runs BEFORE any rule reads an event: this trace holds a frame that returned `Err`, and no disposition, tally or `no exceptions recorded` is printed about it. The retired rung-2 sentence (`exceptions on a rust trace needs the Rust disposition rules`) must not come back for a Rust trace; it survives only for a language with no rule module at all. Every other command on the same trace is unaffected -- `err_flow` gates one command.",
 "meta": {"trace_format": 4,
          "run_id": "$RUN",
          "argv": ["/w/target/debug/deps/demo-abc"],
          "cwd": "/w",
          "env_hash": "0000000000000000",
          "start_ts": 0.0,
          "end_ts": 1.0,
          "exit_status": 101,
          "main_thread_ident": 1,
          "fingerprint_basis": "per-task",
          "truncated_count": 0,
          "source_hashes": {"demo/src/lib.rs": "cccccccccccccccc"},
          "recorder": "sensorium-rt 0.2.0",
          "lang": "rust",
          "capabilities": {"line": false, "locals": false, "return_value": true,
                           "tasks": true, "threads": true, "children": false,
                           "stdin": false, "output": false,
                           "object_identity": false, "refocus": false},
          "threads_started": 0,
          "live_threads": [],
          "caps": {"repr": 200},
          "invocation": "20260101-000000-111111",
          "pid": 100,
          "ppid": 99,
          "exe": "/w/target/debug/deps/demo-abc",
          "toolchain": "rustc 1.96.0 (ac68faa20 2026-05-25)",
          "cargo_args": ["test"],
          "exit_status_basis": "waited",
          "exit_signal": null,
          "units_refused": {"refused": false, "at": null},
          "incomplete": false},
 "codes": [["/w/demo/src/lib.rs", "load", 30],
           ["/w/demo/src/lib.rs", "read_config", 12]],
 "frames": [{"parent": null, "code": 1, "call": 1, "return": 4, "depth": 0,
             "thread": 1, "closed_by": "return", "kind": "function"},
            {"parent": 1, "code": 2, "call": 2, "return": 3, "depth": 1,
             "thread": 1, "closed_by": "return", "kind": "function"}],
 "events": [{"ts": 1000, "thread": 1, "kind": "CALL", "code": 1, "line": 30,
             "payload": {"args": {}, "unread": ["locals"]}, "task": null},
            {"ts": 1100, "thread": 1, "kind": "CALL", "code": 2, "line": 12,
             "payload": {"args": {}, "unread": ["locals"]}, "task": null},
            {"ts": 1200, "thread": 1, "kind": "RETURN", "frame": 2, "code": 2,
             "line": null,
             "payload": {"outcome": "err",
                         "value": {"k": "dbg", "v": "Err(Missing(\"port\"))",
                                   "trunc": false}},
             "task": null},
            {"ts": 1300, "thread": 1, "kind": "RETURN", "frame": 1, "code": 1,
             "line": null,
             "payload": {"outcome": "ok",
                         "value": {"k": "dbg", "v": "None", "trunc": false}},
             "task": null}],
 "fingerprints": "compute",
 "questions": [
   {"id": "exceptions-refuses-a-rust-trace-with-no-err-flow-record",
    "ask": "A Rust recording made before err-flow records existed: does `exceptions` refuse through the capability and say that the RECORDING is what would have to change?",
    "command": ["exceptions", "$RUN"],
    "expect_exit": 3,
    "expect_contains": [
      "REFUSED: exceptions needs err_flow, which recorder sensorium-rt 0.2.0 declares it does not produce (capabilities.err_flow: false); nothing was checked"],
    "expect_absent": ["no exceptions recorded", "SWALLOWED", "raised (",
                      "dispositions:",
                      "needs the Rust disposition rules"]},
   {"id": "the-gate-runs-before-any-rule-sees-the-trace",
    "ask": "The trace holds a frame that returned `Err`. Is anything judged about it, or does the refusal come first?",
    "command": ["exceptions", "$RUN"],
    "expect_exit": 3,
    "expect_count": {"REFUSED": 1},
    "expect_absent": ["ambiguous", "propagated", "returned to the harness",
                      "panicked", "hops:"]},
   {"id": "err-flow-gates-one-command-and-no-other",
    "ask": "Does the missing `err_flow` declaration change what `tree` says about the same trace?",
    "command": ["tree", "$RUN"],
    "expect_exit": 0,
    "expect_line": [["f1 e1", "load()", "-> None"],
                    ["f2 e2", "read_config()", "-> Err(Missing(\"port\"))"]],
    "expect_absent": ["REFUSED", "err_flow"]}]}
